# DNG Deployment Runbook

> Auto-generated by dng-preflight. Review before executing.
>
> **Scope:** {{ config.answers.deployment_scope }}
> **IdP:** {{ config.answers.idp }}
> **Public hostname:** `{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}`
> **DNG minimum version:** {{ config.dng_version_minimum }}

This runbook is ordered to resolve the SAML circular dependency: DNG needs the
IdP's metadata to validate signatures, but the IdP needs DNG's SP metadata to
know who is asking. We bring DNG up with a placeholder primary_auth, export
SP metadata, configure the IdP, then return and complete primary_auth.

---

## Step 0 — DNS records

Publish the records listed in `dns-records.md` **before** running the
installer. The installer refuses to proceed unless `{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}`
resolves.

{% if needs_dns_step_zero %}
> ⚠️  Discovery did not find any A/AAAA records for `{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}`
> on authoritative resolvers (1.1.1.1, 8.8.8.8). The records in
> `dns-records.md` are mandatory at this step.
{% endif %}

## Step 1 — Run the installer

```bash
sudo ./install.sh
```

The installer is idempotent. It will:

1. Verify the host is not domain-joined.
2. Verify `{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}` resolves.
3. Install Docker Engine + Compose plugin if missing.
4. Place `scripted-config.yaml` at `/etc/dng/scripted-config.yaml`.
5. Pull `duosecurity/network-gateway:{{ config.dng_version_minimum }}`.

## Step 2 — Apply firewall rules

```bash
sudo ./firewall.sh
```

This opens public port 443 and restricts admin port 8443 to internal CIDRs.
{% if config.answers.load_balancer %}
The load-balancer CIDRs you specified ({{ lb_cidrs }}) are added to
`load_balancer_cidrs_ips` in the scripted config so the DNG honours
`X-Forwarded-*` headers.
{% endif %}

## Step 3 — Paste TLS material into scripted-config.yaml

{% if tls_kind == 'lets_encrypt_dns01' %}
TLS strategy is **Let's Encrypt (DNS-01)**. DNG will request the cert itself
on first run; no paste step is required. Ensure your DNS provider
({{ config.answers.tls_strategy.dns_provider }}) has the
`_acme-challenge.{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}` TXT records listed in
`dns-records.md` published.
{% else %}
Open `/etc/dng/scripted-config.yaml` and replace the `<<paste contents of …>>`
markers with the actual file bodies:

- `network_gateway.ssl_cert.cert` ← contents of `{{ config.answers.tls_strategy.cert_path }}`
- `network_gateway.ssl_cert.key`  ← contents of `{{ config.answers.tls_strategy.key_path }}`
{% if tls_kind == 'internal_ca' %}
- `network_gateway.ssl_cert.chain` ← contents of `{{ config.answers.tls_strategy.chain_path }}`
  (un-comment the `chain:` key)
{% endif %}

Set file perms to `0600` after editing.
{% endif %}

## Step 4 — First-time DNG bring-up (placeholder primary_auth)

The committed `scripted-config.yaml` ships with placeholder values for
`primary_auth`. That is intentional — we need DNG running to export its SP
metadata before the IdP can be configured.

```bash
sudo docker run --rm \
    -v /etc/dng/scripted-config.yaml:/config/scripted-config.yaml:ro \
    duosecurity/network-gateway:{{ config.dng_version_minimum }} \
    init
sudo docker compose -f /etc/dng/docker-compose.yml up -d
```

> Wait ~30 seconds for the container to become healthy.

## Step 5 — Export DNG SP metadata

```bash
curl -fsSL https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/metadata/ \
    -o dng-sp-metadata.xml
```

Hand `dng-sp-metadata.xml` to your IdP administrator.

## Step 6 — Configure the IdP

{% if config.answers.idp == 'duo_sso' %}
In **Duo SSO**, create a Generic SAML Service Provider with:
- ACS URL: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/acs/`
- Entity ID: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/metadata/`
- SLO URL: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/sls/`
{% elif config.answers.idp == 'okta' %}
In **Okta**, add a new SAML 2.0 application with:
- Single sign-on URL: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/acs/`
- Audience URI (SP Entity ID): `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/metadata/`
- Application username: Email
{% elif config.answers.idp == 'entra_id' %}
In **Microsoft Entra ID**, add an Enterprise Application using SAML:
- Identifier (Entity ID): `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/metadata/`
- Reply URL: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/acs/`
- Logout URL: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/sls/`
{% elif config.answers.idp == 'adfs' %}
In **AD FS**, add a Relying Party Trust:
- Federation metadata: paste the contents of `dng-sp-metadata.xml`
- Or, manually: Entity ID `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/metadata/`,
  ACS `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/acs/`.
{% else %}
For a generic SAML 2.0 IdP, configure the SP using:
- Entity ID: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/metadata/`
- ACS URL: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/acs/`
- SLO URL: `https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}/sls/`
{% endif %}

After the IdP is configured, export its metadata (an XML file) and note:

- IdP entity ID
- IdP SSO URL
- IdP signing certificate (PEM block from `<ds:X509Certificate>`)

## Step 7 — Import IdP metadata into DNG

Open `/etc/dng/scripted-config.yaml` and fill in `primary_auth`:

```yaml
primary_auth:
    entity_id: '<IdP entity ID from Step 6>'
    single_signon_url: '<IdP SSO URL from Step 6>'
    signing_cert: |
        -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
        ...
        -----END CERTIFICATE-----
```

Restart DNG:

```bash
sudo docker compose -f /etc/dng/docker-compose.yml restart
```

## Step 8 — First-login password reset

The placeholder `network_gateway.password` in `scripted-config.yaml` is for
config-time use only. On first admin login at
`https://{{ config.answers.public_hostname }}:8443/`, DNG requires you to set a
new password via shell access to the container:

```bash
sudo docker exec -it dng /opt/dng/reset_admin_password
```

